      "title": "TCP Three-Way Handshake",
      "content": "TCP establishes a reliable connection using a three-way handshake. The client sends a SYN segment, the server replies with SYN-ACK, and the client responds with ACK. After these three steps both sides have synchronized sequence numbers and the connection is established.",
